Hmm, the amalgamated geography and mythology of Howard's Hyborian Age 
world can easily be confusing, I don't think that Cimmeria should be 
linked to Scandinavia/Iceland firstmost.

* Cimmeria in the real world was situated somewhere in the area of 
southwestern Russia - northern Middle East. There was a Cimmerian people 
living in this area ca 700 BC, which later have given name to a 
continent plate thought to have ended up in about the same area.
* Cimmeria in the Hyborian Age roughly corresponds to old Celtic 
Britain.
* Crom in the Hyborian Age seems to be inspired by Crom Cruach, a major 
god in Celtic Mythology.
* Crom in the real world has nothing to do with Norse mythology (of 
Scandinavia and Iceland).
* Note also that Conan's name is Irish and that he is from Cimmeria.

So Crom - and Cimmeria - is linked to old Celtic Britain and it's 
mythology, and not to Scandinavia, Iceland or the Norse mythology.

There seems to a common misconception stemming from the first Conan 
movie where Crom is spoken of as a ruler of Valhalla. IIRC this does not 
match up well with the books.

